This version of LegoBlast is a Work-in-progress version... REALLY !
The game appearance could change radically, screen resolution could
change, a lot of ideas have to be coded... And when i can't code,
i'm thinging about really-fun and new modes. I found pipes idea 2 weeks
ago, and i've a pacman-mode which could be cool...

I won't delete and rewrite thousand lines of code,
but everything else could be done.

  So, you'll find the executable file of the game called "LegoBlast" :
You said me that a commercialisation of this concept isn't possible,
due to the appearance of the Lego firm in multimedia, 
but we don't want to redraw all the guys if you aren't interested a bit
by this game. (Logic) (If we put this game on aminet, i think we won't have 
license problems....) 

The game is coded 100% ASM.

This is a very-first preview.
- Program is far to be finished, no menu yet.
  In appearance it could seem to be soon-finished : We can play, 
  sounds, music, etc... But I have a LOT of things to code.
  For example two weeks ago i coded&"drawed" (cloned) bomb-freezing
  in blue instead of a normal bomb with no animation. This was 
  a little detail in my TO-DO things, but it took me time... And this 
  morning i finished pipes...
- We only have one music for the instance. (We have some conversion
  problems with P6. We must modify musics with protracker...it's not my problem,
  but music-man one!)
- Each Graphic could be redrawn,(Ground, Walls) and perhaps passed in Hires mode.
  (The Hires mode would be exactly the same speed, because a Move.l takes 
  the same time as a Move.w (if the Move.l is long word aligned, of course).
  I just code "one-palette-per-level" mode, but i hadn't enough time yet to
  create ingenious levels. Since i've made a level editor, everything
  can be easyly modified... I think that many level will be reworked.
  All the bonus and blocs we done aren't "freezed" : Everyone in the
  group often modifies one bonus to improve it, or sometimes someone
  finds a new icon-idea and draws it ... So nothing is freezed.
- Most of the sounds must be changed. (For example bonus-get, dead ...) 
- I had code pipes. I think this will add a great think
  to the game. This will permit to attack a player from 2 ways 
  with one explosion... And it could be very beautiful with glass-pipes, 
  when we'll see explosions in transparent. (I'll surely have to use
  a seventh planar, to do exactly the same thing as a EHB mode, 
  for all transparent-glasses mode)
- Level editor isn't finished yet (AMOS). I continue it every week...
  Two weeks ago, i've included teleport-handling in editor. 
  Last week, i've included bonus probabilities.
  This week, i've included pipes handling.
  When it will be totally finished, i'll have to think about 
  the possibility of using external levels during execution. (For the
  instance all levels are included during compilation).
- Since the executable is about to become a very big file, we'll surely
  have to make a multi-file game, instead of a one-file one.
  (This could allow to the user the possibility of changing samples,
  so it could be a great idea)
- I must take real screen initialisations for all Workbench resolutions from
  another code. (Not hard but i've a lot of things to do before... ;-) )
- For the instance, the game uses a 320x256x64 and a 640x18x64 screens,
  but it's in our intention to modify it to get a 640x274x64 screen,
  (so all in hires), and perhaps more than 64 colours if needed.
  The changement between Lowres and Hires mode will need:
  - to double all graphics, so it will double the graphics size in memory
    (Not really a problem since all blocs take about 50 ko)
  - to modify all graphics routines, Move.L instead of Move.W, and
    the most difficult due to a lack of registers : The planars offsets
    will be doubled, so i'll have to adress all planars in long mode...
    (Move.L D0,(A0,D0.L) Instead of Move.L D0,2*SizePlanar(A0) ) 
- Cobalt and Black Angel recently started an animation project of a new guy,
  in the case we can't use lego-guys animations... 
- For the instance, most of the bonus are the common ones, but we found
  a few ideas to use a maximum of game's possibilities.
    For example, the "superman" mode, the "nervous" mode, new blocs,
  as the pipe, at 90° or 180°, which modifies explosions' direction,
  or the "bouncers" which affects bombs (and players ?)...
  We also wanted to make automatic-ground, which drives bombs and players
  in any directions.............
  I also though : a ventilator, which could be able to "push" bombs...

We have a LOT of ideas and projects... some could be very great...


So the executable is here to show you the actual progress of the project.

Things that Works:
- 320*256*64 colors
- 4 players
- Teleportations
- Bomb freezing
- Bomb pushing
- "Bomb movement energy handling" :   A -> BCDEF will do ABCDE -> F
- End of level board reducing
- Setting for each level the probability of each bonus :
  70% of chances to see an empty bloc when a wall is blasted
  10% of chances to get a bomb bonus when i blast a wall, 
  20% of chances to get a water bonus etc etc...
  This permits to enable/disable bonus when we want :
  For example if i don't want bonus in level 4, i do :
  100% of chances to get an empty bloc when i blast a wall 
- I'm coding pipes.
- ALL variables are initialised at the beginning of each level, so you can
  change level during bomb explosions with no problems...
- And ALL the things i can't remember... the best way to find every 
  things is to play during at least one hour... 
- One palette per level (permits "worlds")
- One explosion per level (could be great with cool explosions)

Personnaly, i played on a standard A1200 and on a BlizzardIV (mine),
and the game NEVER reboot during game.

The game is fast enough even on a standard A1200, but i've not tested
pipes on it. Indeed, each collision of an explosion with a pipe 
duplicates it, so with lame levels, you can produce slowings easily ;
I made a level in which the explosions are duplicated in loop :
with ONE bomb, i made my Amiga slowing down...
But if levels are clever done, these case would not be produced.


For information, the little time before game starting is done
to wait disk activity when i "compile+run" my prog, so i can leave it.
